{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Lift up your eyes on high. Who created these.</b> The created beings that are there, and who brings them forth every day by their host's number — this corresponds to the visible ones. It is also possible that it alludes to the wandering stars, for each one has a known number before HaShem, but the people of the East and all the astrologers to this day cannot determine the number of each one's outgoing. Or it speaks of the number of the stars that are in the uppermost sphere, for there is no ability to know their number." "<b>Abundant in power.</b> That He possesses, and that He is mighty in strength." "<b>Not one is missing.</b> The meaning concerns the number, or the substance of each star — it never dies. Now איש is like עצם, as in והאיש גבריאל (Daniel 9:21)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 40, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:16.769453616Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}